    "name": "Prune Plum",
    "description": "<p>Since prune plums are likely to mold readily after picking, the farmers have opted not to rinse these before sending them along. Plums have a natural bloom (whitish layer on the skin...that's not ash). We recommend rinsing them at home prior to eating to remove any larger particles of ash that might have stuck from the fires.</p>",
